  "description": "Waiariki is the Māori electorate of the Bay of Plenty, covering population centres such as Tauranga, Whakatāne, and Rotorua. The seat is held by current Te Pāti Māori co-leader Rawiri Waititi who won in 2023 with 21,500 votes and 36.7% of the party vote. Since its establishment, the seat has been a stronghold for Te Pāti Māori. A Labour candidate has only won once since 2005. \n\n",
